    <div class=3D"o-blocks">
        <p>An accompanying catalogue offers comprehensive look at the work =
of the groundbreaking photographer, foregrounding her importance as a surre=
alist artist. Essays draw on new archival research and explore every aspect=
 of Miller=E2=80=99s career, from her early years in Paris, New York, and C=
airo to her wartime journalism and late portraits. Additionally, the Britis=
h novelist, playwright, and poet Deborah Levy offers a personal reflection =
on Miller and her art. <a target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer nofo=
llow" href=3D"https://shop.artic.edu/collections/lee-miller-fearless/produc=
ts/292256">Learn more</a>.</p>

